From 7faa9ff0766935c0ecdfed29bf0e5b098b622baa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:13:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: carry the tool-call anchor across upstream's
 same-n_tokens checkpoint supersede (W1 collision C077)

Upstream 5d806aa25 supersedes a checkpoint at the same n_tokens instead of appending a duplicate; the loop ignored our R31/M15 anchor flag, so a plain save at the anchor's position erased the thinning-exempt restore point. The list bookkeeping moves into server-ckpt-storage.h (server_ckpt_list_make_room) and the server and test-ctx-checkpoint-storage now call the same copy; the test's private copy had drifted from the union. The superseding entry is the same restore point, so it inherits the anchor. Test: 14/14 PASS; with the carry line disabled the two C077 checks FAIL (RED probe).

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-296
Lane: lane-296
---
 tests/test-ctx-checkpoint-storage.cpp | 38 +++++++++++--------
 tools/server/server-ckpt-storage.h    | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/server/server-context.cpp       | 53 +++++++--------------------
 3 files changed, 85 insertions(+), 56 deletions(-)

